Hi!

Just ascended my first game... here's a manually-generated dumplog
(couldn't install the dumplog patch): http://pastebin.com/AeKW4yar
I was playing a chaotic male elven wizard.

It was quite lucky, I found a 0:2 wand of wishing on dungeon level 3
in a shop... I wished for +2 SDSM, charging, +2 speed boots, MKoT, and
a magic marker, so i had about -15 AC quite early. Some levels deeper,
I found a Jewelery and found most useful rings (except conflict) there
using the Identify spell. I gained Frost Brand, Magicbane and
Stormbringer (which cost me many alignment points :p) through
sacrificing, and enchanted them both to +6.
Descending into the VoTD, i found my bones from the last game, where i
got disintegrated by a black dragon (forgot to put on my SDSM --
disintegrated me twice with one beam, so "oLS was useless) and could
further lower my AC by looting the stuff there. I then wished for an
Amulet of Life Saving (I'm paranoid you know), several markers,
genociding L, h and ;, and later writing a spellbook of finger of
death (for some reason, my god wouldn't crown me, and I also didn't
have create monster for altar scumming).
I played Gehennom quite fast, as usual (magic mapping, dig a straight
way with a pick-axe, descend, repeat), not killing much except Orcus
and Jubilex.
Finding the Vibrating Square took me a while, but killing the Wizard
of Yendor with FoD was a piece of cake (obviously). I almost died in
the Sanctum (the priest hits hard, especially if you only have about
100 HP!), but I could escape from the crowd of monsters (only about 15
HP and no healing left) using a cursed gain level potion (after
picking up the amulet).

My AC was now -29, including 4 points of divine protection. Ascending
mainly with the Teleport spell, i got stuck in Beelzebub's Level, and
spent my last non-wrest wish on a chickatrice corpse, turning them all
into nice statues. I accidentally forgot to put on my levitation ring,
and fell into a spiked pit, which took away one of my Life Saving
amulets (luckily, i had one more from Vlads). I used the cockatrice-
tactics again to make a nice forest of troll statues in the troll-
level because they were really annoying me (this time with
levitation). After the Wizard of Yendor appeared and I killed him
within 2 turns, I noticed I was missing my +6 Magicbane -- I've had no
idea where it could be. Deciding not to search it because I still had
+6 Stormbringer, I continued climbing up.
The rest of the ascension until the planes was really easy, as I had
plenty of food and could just teleport to the upstairs in every non-
teleport level. The Wizard appeared once or twice, but was always
quickly sent away by my Finger of Death spell.
The plane of Earth turned out to be very easy (after giving the pink @
the bit of FoD it deserved), using cursed gold detection to find the
portal.
The plane of Air was a bit dangerous because of the air elementals,
but I either FoD'd them or teleported them away after casting Slow
Monster.
Fire turned out to be difficult first, because I wasn't confused when
reading the scroll I had saved for that level, so I didn't know where
the portal was -- until some of the monsters stepped in, which really
saved me. :)
Water was a bit confusing, but I randomly stepped into the portal
after a few hundred moves or so.
On the astral plane, I promptly stumbled into Death after about ten
moves, but luckily he was slower than me, so I could easily escape. I
then put on my Conflict ring. I went to the altar on the right first,
which was wrong -- it was the neutral one. Of course, I went to the
top one next, which was lawful -- but luckily, I had found an helm of
opposite alignment in the castle armory. That's where I ascended.

Of course, there was much luck in this game (Wand of wishing! :P), so
I think there's still some stuff left to learn.  But neverthereless --
won is won, right? :)

